<title>TURKEY: Turk central bank reserve up $566 mln in Sept 6 wk.</title>
<headline>Turk central bank reserve up $566 mln in Sept 6 wk.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $566 million to $16.781 billion in the week ended on September 6.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Aug 30	  Aug 30	   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve  16.781	  16.215	   12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve    1.383	   1.383	    1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve  18.164	  17.598	   13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose $128 million to $26.977 billion in the week ending August 23, the bank said.</p>
<p>It said Turkey serviced $151.93 million of state foreign debt in the period of September 2-11.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
